 "admissions_overview": {
  "summary": "In Ghana each public and private university sets its own admission and runs its own application; there is no single national placement for universities. Applicants are mainly assessed on their WASSCE results (core subjects plus relevant electives), and universities publish programme-specific entry requirements, with mature-student, diploma/HND and international routes as well. The Ghana Tertiary Education Commission (GTEC) regulates and accredits tertiary institutions and has directed that entrance tests must not replace the WASSCE-based minimum entry requirements.",
  "official_url": "https://gtec.edu.gh",
  "notes": "Application windows, vouchers, programme availability and grades required for popular programmes change every year. Check the admissions page of each university (and gtec.edu.gh for accredited institutions) before applying."
 },
